=== T-103
{
  "phase": "read",
  "turns": 12,
  "cost": 0.25,
  "verdict": {
    "verdict": "not_a_bug",
    "summary": "T-103 asks for tail -f style follow mode. This is a feature request for functionality the project deliberately excluded, not a defect. SPEC.md section 14 \"Non-goals for v1\" explicitly lists \"Live tailing (--follow)\" among decisions that were \"considered and deferred deliberately... so they are not re-litigated as oversights,\" with the rationale that it needs an event loop plus rotation detection and makes aggregation non-terminating. The code matches that spec: the CLI argument parser defines no --follow/-f flag, and the reader opens each input as a one-shot handle (stdin, plain file, or gzip) streamed to EOF with no watch or re-read path. So the observed behavior is documented and intentional; no code fix applies. Implementing follow mode would be new architecture (event loop, rotation detection, and a decision about what aggregation means over an unbounded stream), and the spec names multiline records rather than follow mode as the first v2 candidate \u2014 so any roadmap commitment is a product call, but the triage question of bug-vs-documented is settled by the spec.",
    "evidence": [
      "SPEC.md:719-722",
      "SPEC.md:727-728",
      "src/logsift/cli.py:80-128",
      "src/logsift/cli.py:127",
      "src/logsift/reader.py:87-97",
      "SPEC.md:724-726"
    ]
  }
}
